            <ArticleTitle>Painful ophthalmologic disorders and eye pain for the neurologist.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>75-97</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Neurologists should be aware of the following causes of eye pain: (1)ocular and orbital disorders with or without visible pathology of the eye (eg,redness, corneal opacity, or proptosis); (2) ophthalmologic syndromes associated with headache; and (3) headache syndromes associated with ophthalmologic findings.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
